FixedRateIrm::setMarket(address)
├── given market is already nonzero
│   └── when the new address is zero the existing market or another address
│       ├── it should revert with IrmMarketAlreadySet
│       └── it should preserve market and IRState and emit no events
└── given market is zero
    ├── when caller is owner another address or the supplied market
    │   └── it should allow permissionless binding to an EOA without interface validation
    ├── when supplied market is zero
    │   ├── it should accept zero and initialize the state while leaving market unbound
    │   └── it should allow repeated zero binding followed by a nonzero binding
    ├── when timestamp is zero or type(uint48).max
    │   └── it should accept the exact timestamp
    ├── when timestamp exceeds type(uint48).max on the first binding
    │   └── it should truncate lastUpdate to the low 48 bits without reverting
    ├── it should preserve the configured borrowRate
    ├── it should store the supplied market and preserve owner
    ├── it should set lastUpdate to uint48 of the current timestamp
    └── it should emit exactly one IRStateUpdated with the resulting rate and timestamp
